  "description": "ITEWEK crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C96 H146 Dy9 N8 O34 1+,3(C1 H4 O1),H1 O1 1-. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.466-5.035 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 88.71-178.87°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy9L8(μ3-OH)8(μ4-OH)2(CH3OH)8](OH)(CH3OH)3 (L = 2-((1-hydroxybutan-2-ylimino)methyl)phenolate; CCDC cation C96H146Dy9N8O34 with 3 MeOH and OH-; EA calcd as C101H160Dy9N8O41). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
